# A call into the kernel from TypeScript, as check/judge.ts's `kernel` made it before item term-self-host-001-0072:
# the step runs, and when it raises, the unfold fuel is put back to what it was at the call, the value the original's
# `finally` chain restored on every conversion that unfolded (nothing inside the kernel catches such a raise).
#
# The answer says how the step ended. A `failure` whose note names a kernel error (`kernel-type:` for the original's
# `TypeError`, `kernel-fault:` for a plain `Error`, check/judging.tree's header) comes back as `judge-raised` with the
# raise itself and its message without the prefix, so the face throws that same raise again as the original's class:
# a raise is reused, never rebuilt, because the elaborator throws and catches thousands a program (traps.md T039). A
# `failure` with any other note comes back with kind `<>`, and the face throws it as it came. Any other raise passes
# on from here as it came, the fuel put back first.
#
# Unlike check/judging.tree's `kernel-call`, nothing is turned into an answer the caller must read: `decline:` stays a
# raise, which check/elaborate.ts turns into its `Decline`.

load @term/base/exception
  find exception
  find failure

load @term/base/text
  find substring
  find starts-with

load ./judging
  find judge-state

form judge-outcome
  case judge-done
    link value, like unknown
  case judge-raised
    link raised, like unknown
    link kind, like text
    link message, like text

task run-in-kernel
  take st, like judge-state
  take step
    like task
      like unknown
      halt failure
  like judge-outcome

  save fuel, st/unfold-fuel
  fork
    mark unsafe
    save value, step()
    back
      make judge-done
        bind value, value
  halt take
    take problem
    save st/unfold-fuel, fuel
    sift problem
      case failure
        link note
        fork test, starts-with(note, <kernel-type:>)
          hold
            back
              make judge-raised
                bind raised, problem
                bind kind, <type>
                bind message, substring(note, 12, note/length)
        fork test, starts-with(note, <kernel-fault:>)
          hold
            back
              make judge-raised
                bind raised, problem
                bind kind, <fault>
                bind message, substring(note, 13, note/length)
        back
          make judge-raised
            bind raised, problem
            bind kind, <>
            bind message, note
  back
    make judge-raised
      bind raised, <unreachable>
      bind kind, <>
      bind message, <unreachable>
